cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use praatfan-gpl in published work, please cite it, and please also
  cite Praat (Boersma & Weenink, "Praat: doing phonetics by computer",
  https://www.praat.org): praatfan-gpl reimplements Praat's analyses from
  Praat's source code, and was made to match Praat as exposed by parselmouth
  0.4.7 (Praat 6.1.38).
type: software
title: "Praatfan-gpl: a reimplementation in Rust of a number of Praat functions"
authors:
  - family-names: Cohen Priva
    given-names: Uriel
repository-code: "https://github.com/ucpresearch/praatfan-core-rs"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/praatfan-gpl/"
license: GPL-3.0-only
keywords:
  - Praat
  - phonetics
  - acoustic analysis
  - pitch
  - formants
